<% content_for :title, "Sales Tax Calculator — whizwheel" %>

<%#
  Sales Tax calculator page (spec issue #252, DESIGN.md BLEND) — a solve-for-X calculator over
  three related figures: the before-tax price (B), the sales-tax rate (%), and the after-tax
  price (A), sitting on one relationship A = B × (1 + rate/100). Given any TWO, solve for the
  third (and always report the tax amount). A required `mode` picker names WHICH figure is the
  unknown; the form shows only the two GIVEN fields for the chosen mode. The form posts over
  Turbo and re-renders the #result region in place; it works WITHOUT JS — the server validates
  exactly the selected mode's two required fields and re-renders the result fragment. The
  sales_tax_controller is pure polish: it reveals only the active mode's two fields (disabling
  the rest so they're never posted), lifts the chosen segment, and swaps the helper line.

  Mode-picker choice (DESIGN.md §4 "Mode picker"): THREE modes (N = 3), all SHORT labels
  ("After-tax price" / "Before-tax price" / "Tax rate"). The §4 rule routes N ≤ 3 with short
  labels to the SEGMENTED CONTROL (the connected horizontal track), not the option list. It
  stays a native radio <fieldset>/<legend> posting a single-select inputs[mode]; a helper line
  under the segments names what the active mode solves. (Structural twin of VAT #255 — keep
  parallel.)

  Layout per DESIGN.md §3 — an input column + a results panel (≈380px 1fr), collapsing to one
  column on mobile. Spacing scale ("targets not minimums"):
    • stacked fields → space-y-5
    • major blocks within the card (mode → fields → submit) → mt-8 (Section tier)
    • column gutters / card padding → gap-8 / p-7–p-8 (Layout tier)
%>

<header class="max-w-2xl">
  <p class="text-[11px] font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.12em] text-accent">Financial</p>
  <h1 class="mt-2 text-4xl font-extrabold tracking-[-0.035em] text-ink">Sales Tax Calculator</h1>
  <p class="mt-3 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-muted">
    Solve a sales-tax problem from any two of the three figures — the
    <span class="font-semibold text-ink">before-tax price</span>, the
    <span class="font-semibold text-ink">tax rate</span>, or the
    <span class="font-semibold text-ink">after-tax price</span> — and get the tax amount and the
    missing value. Every figure is computed server-side.
  </p>
</header>

<div class="mt-8 grid grid-cols-1 gap-8 lg:grid-cols-[380px_1fr]">
  <%# ── Input column ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────── %>
  <section class="rounded-[18px] border border-border bg-surface p-7 shadow-[0_10px_34px_rgba(150,110,80,0.12)] sm:p-8">
    <%= form_with url: "/calculators/sales_tax", scope: :inputs, method: :post,
          data: { controller: "sales-tax" } do |f| %>

      <%# Mode picker — segmented control (DESIGN.md §4 "Mode picker"): three short labels →
          a connected horizontal track of full-width segments, NOT the option list (reserved
          for N ≥ 4 or multi-word labels). The accessible control is a native radio
          <fieldset>/<legend> posting inputs[mode]; each radio is visually-hidden (peer sr-only)
          and paired to a styled <label for>. The chosen segment lifts to surface white with no
          JS via peer:checked. A helper line below names what the active mode solves — one line
          per mode, the active one shown (the no-JS baseline shows all three stacked; Stimulus
          reveals only the active line). %>
      <fieldset>
        <legend class="field-label">Solve for</legend>
        <div class="mt-1.5 flex gap-1 rounded-[11px] border border-border-input bg-bg p-1">
          <% sales_tax_modes.each_with_index do |m, i| %>
            <%= f.radio_button :mode, m[:value],
                  checked: i.zero?,
                  class: "peer sr-only",
                  data: { sales_tax_target: "modeInput", action: "sales-tax#select" } %>
            <%= f.label :mode, m[:label], value: m[:value],
                  class: "direction-pill",
                  data: { sales_tax_target: "modeSegment", mode: m[:value] } %>
          <% end %>
        </div>
        <%# Helper lines — one per mode, naming what it solves. The active mode's line is shown;
            Stimulus hides the rest. No-JS baseline shows all three stacked (still legible). %>
        <div class="mt-2 space-y-1">
          <% sales_tax_modes.each do |m| %>
            <p class="text-xs leading-relaxed text-muted"
               data-sales-tax-target="modeHelper" data-mode="<%= m[:value] %>">
              <%= m[:helper] %>
            </p>
          <% end %>
        </div>
      </fieldset>

      <%# Fields. Stacked tier: space-y-5 down the column (DESIGN.md §3). Each field declares the
          modes that GIVE it via data-sales-tax-modes (space-separated); Stimulus shows only the
          active mode's two fields and disables the rest so the solved-for field is never posted
          (the no-JS baseline shows all three — the server reads only the mode's two required
          fields). Each input carries its $/% affix on the Affix tier (gap-2). %>
      <div class="mt-8 space-y-5">
        <%# Before-tax price — given in the `after` and `rate` modes. $ leading affix. %>
        <div data-sales-tax-target="field" data-sales-tax-modes="after rate">
          <%= f.label :before_tax_price, "Before-tax price", class: "field-label", for: "inputs_before_tax_price" %>
          <div class="mt-1.5 flex items-center gap-2">
            <span class="text-sm font-bold text-label" aria-hidden="true">$</span>
            <%= f.number_field :before_tax_price, id: "inputs_before_tax_price", step: "any", inputmode: "decimal",
                  min: "0", placeholder: "0.00", class: "field-input" %>
          </div>
        </div>

        <%# After-tax price — given in the `before` and `rate` modes. $ leading affix. %>
        <div data-sales-tax-target="field" data-sales-tax-modes="before rate">
          <%= f.label :after_tax_price, "After-tax price", class: "field-label", for: "inputs_after_tax_price" %>
          <div class="mt-1.5 flex items-center gap-2">
            <span class="text-sm font-bold text-label" aria-hidden="true">$</span>
            <%= f.number_field :after_tax_price, id: "inputs_after_tax_price", step: "any", inputmode: "decimal",
                  min: "0", placeholder: "0.00", class: "field-input" %>
          </div>
        </div>

        <%# Tax rate — given in the `after` and `before` modes. % trailing affix. %>
        <div data-sales-tax-target="field" data-sales-tax-modes="after before">
          <%= f.label :rate, "Tax rate", class: "field-label", for: "inputs_rate" %>
          <div class="mt-1.5 flex items-center gap-2">
            <%= f.number_field :rate, id: "inputs_rate", step: "any", inputmode: "decimal",
                  min: "0", placeholder: "0", class: "field-input" %>
            <span class="text-sm font-bold text-label" aria-hidden="true">%</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <%# Submit — Section tier above; primary coral button (DESIGN.md §4). %>
      <%= f.submit "Calculate",
            class: "mt-8 w-full cursor-pointer rounded-[13px] bg-primary px-4 py-3 text-sm font-semibold text-surface shadow-sm transition-opacity hover:opacity-90 focus:outline-none focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-accent" %>
    <% end %>
  </section>

  <%# ── Results panel (the Turbo target) ─────────────────────────────────── %>
  <section id="result" aria-live="polite">
    <%= render "calculators/result", calc: nil %>
  </section>
</div>
